        "timestamp": 1789921350.5785222,
        "text": "The first command to diagnose connection refused from a local HTTP server is:\n\n```bash\nnc -vz <host> <port>\n```\n\nThat runs against the real network path and reports the specific reason if the socket cannot be established.\n\nA second, more useful diagnostic is:\n\n```bash\nss -tlnp | grep <host>:<port>\n```\n\nThat confirms whether the process is bound to the interface, listening on TCP, and which PID owns it \u2014 a prerequisite before a connection can be refused."
